# Carol

Hello, I am Carol. I act as a worker, and my job in this session is to write
down how a distance is turned into a logic, in the methodology, and to prove
its rules in Lean. My session is `strange-loops-in-hmd-49`.

## Report, 02:05

**Goal.** The user asked for the method by which a distance between two
things is read as an implication, written into the methodology in proper
logical notation, with Lean proofs kept in the scripts folder.

**Done.**

- [From distance to logic](../../../methodology/distance-to-logic.hmd): the
  definitions, the notation (`a ⊑ b`, `a ≡ b`, `a ⊑ε b`), the rules, the
  reading of the predicates, the step from a belief to a cost, derivation as
  a chain, and what the method does not do.
- [DistanceLogic.lean](../../../scripts/lean/DistanceLogic.lean), with
  `lakefile.toml` and `lean-toolchain` beside it. It uses core Lean only.
  `lake build` passes at 02:00 with no warning and no `sorry`.

What Lean proves: entailment is a preorder; the costs of two steps add; a
chain of asserted steps bounds the distance it spans; a preorder is exactly a
distance with two values; a symmetric distance cannot tell entailment from
equivalence; a signed distance makes every two things comparable.

**In progress.** Nothing.

**Next.** Nothing, unless the user asks. Two things the user may want are
under "Needs".

